WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.143
A growth cone touches a cell just before it turns.

2
00:00:07.043 --> 00:00:08.643
Does it need that cell to make the turn?

3
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:12.653
The worked case is the leg of a grasshopper embryo.

4
00:00:13.783 --> 00:00:17.883
Near the tip of the leg sits a pair of sensory neurons called Ti1.

5
00:00:18.883 --> 00:00:22.483
They send the first axons toward the central nervous system.

6
00:00:23.343 --> 00:00:26.503
In the far part of the leg, no earlier axons lie ahead.

7
00:00:27.483 --> 00:00:28.923
So they are pioneers there.

8
00:00:29.923 --> 00:00:32.903
Nearer the body, they join stretches pioneered by other neurons.

9
00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.627
Their route has several turns.

10
00:00:36.527 --> 00:00:40.487
At some sit young neurons that the growth cones touch just before turning.

11
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:45.077
At one of these turns sits a pair of cells called Cx1.

12
00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.507
But touching is not needing.

13
00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:52.087
The growth cones might touch Cx1 and turn there for some other reason.

14
00:00:53.117 --> 00:00:57.577
David Bentley and Michael Caudy asked the direct question, in 1983.

15
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.940
They selectively destroyed the Cx1 cells before the pioneer growth cones arrived.

16
00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:08.313
If Cx1 is only on the way, the route should look normal.

17
00:01:09.153 --> 00:01:11.773
If it is needed, the route should go wrong at that turn.

18
00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:13.733
Which happened?

19
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:22.153
The pioneers failed to take the normal route.

20
00:01:22.973 --> 00:01:25.193
They sent branches in abnormal directions.

21
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:29.043
At this turn, the growth cones need Cx1.

22
00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:35.037
The conclusion is narrow, and that is its strength.

23
00:01:35.937 --> 00:01:38.637
At this turn, in this preparation, these cells are needed.

24
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.670
It does not say whether Cx1 provides adhesion or a signal.

25
00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.200
Later work by Caudy and Bentley showed that the full route is built from several

26
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.200
legs.

27
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.510
Some legs are read from guideposts.

28
00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:56.150
Others are read from boundaries in the surrounding tissue.

29
00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.163
So a guidepost is one important cue among several.

30
00:02:01.183 --> 00:02:04.783
A choice point is a place where the growth cone picks its next path.

31
00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:08.333
A guidepost cell is one way to guide that choice.

32
00:02:09.317 --> 00:02:13.837
Remove one guidepost, and the pioneers lose their normal route at that turn.
